        ["What does PEEP primarily do in a ventilated patient?", ["Keeps alveoli open at the end of exhalation", "Sets the number of mandatory breaths", "Measures arterial blood pressure", "Determines tidal volume for each breath"], "PEEP maintains positive pressure at end expiration to prevent alveolar collapse."],
        ["A patient's pulse oximeter reads 82% during walking, but the waveform is erratic and the patient is talking comfortably. What is the BEST next step?", ["Check the probe and signal while assessing the patient", "Stop and call a rapid response immediately", "Increase oxygen to the maximum available", "Ignore the reading because the patient feels fine"], "A poor waveform suggests artifact; confirm the signal while still watching for clinical signs of hypoxemia."]
