        ["A ventilated patient on rising, high-dose vasopressors with a new uncontrolled arrhythmia is referred for mobility. What is the MOST appropriate action?", ["Defer active mobilization and discuss with the team", "Stand the patient to improve blood pressure", "Walk the patient with the ventilator attached", "Perform resistance training to the legs"], "Hemodynamic instability places the patient in a high-risk category for active mobility."],
        ["During edge-of-bed sitting, a ventilated patient's SpO2 drops substantially, he becomes tachypneic, and he signals distress. What is the BEST action?", ["Stop, lie him back, and notify RT", "Continue sitting to build tolerance", "Stand him to improve lung expansion", "Increase sitting time to 30 minutes"], "Significant desaturation with distress is a stop criterion; involve RT."],
        ["A spouse of an ICU patient reports insomnia, anxiety, and intrusive memories since the admission. Which concept BEST describes this?", ["PICS-F", "ICU-acquired weakness", "Critical illness myopathy", "Hospital-associated disability"], "Family members can develop psychological effects called PICS-F."],
        ["Which statement about early mobilization of mechanically ventilated patients is MOST accurate?", ["With screening, it is safe and can improve function", "It is contraindicated while any ventilator is in use", "It increases ICU mortality in all patients", "It should start only after ICU discharge"], "Studies show early mobilization is safe with appropriate screening and can improve function and delirium."]
